---
description: Put a 1-2 line English note at the top of every source file so a reviewer can see what it does
alwaysApply: true
---

# English file blurb (for the developer reviewing the code)

When you **create or substantially edit** a source, config, or docs file, open it with a 1–2 line English comment (or a short markdown sentence under the title) that says what the file is and what it does. Keep that blurb updated if the file's role changes.

This is for humans reading the repo — not for crawled site pages. Never add `english_summary` or similar fields under `data/`.
